{"step_index":229,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T18:29:43Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nمش عارف في مشكلة في الـ run، الكود بتاعك مش مظبوط. لو أنت رحت الـ folder بتاع Pharmacy بتاع ChatGPT، هتلاقيهم الكود اللي هو عامله شغال تمام كويس. هبعت لك الكود بتاع OpenCode اللي هو المفروض نستخدمه، فمش عارف في المشكلة. بتاع ChatGPT كان مطلع نتيجة، أنت هنا مش راضي يطلع، بيجي لي 0 match و error وبتاع، مش عارف. \n\nimport requests\r\nimport json\r\n\r\n# First API call with reasoning\r\nresponse = requests.post(\r\n  url=\"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions\",\r\n  headers={\r\n    \"Authorization\": \"Bearer <OPENROUTER_API_KEY>\",\r\n    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\r\n  },\r\n  data=json.dumps({\r\n    \"model\": \"openrouter/free\",\r\n    \"messages\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"role\": \"user\",\r\n          \"content\": \"How many r's are in the word 'strawberry'?\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n    \"reasoning\": {\"enabled\": True}\r\n  })\r\n)\r\n\r\n# Extract the assistant message with reasoning_details\r\nresponse = response.json()\r\nresponse = response['choices'][0]['message']\r\n\r\n# Preserve the assistant message with reasoning_details\r\nmessages = [\r\n  {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"How many r's are in the word 'strawberry'?\"},\r\n  {\r\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n    \"content\": response.get('content'),\r\n    \"reasoning_details\": response.get('reasoning_details')  # Pass back unmodified\r\n  },\r\n  {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Are you sure? Think carefully.\"}\r\n]\r\n\r\n# Second API call - model continues reasoning from where it left off\r\nresponse2 = requests.post(\r\n  url=\"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions\",\r\n  data=json.dumps({\r\n    \"model\": \"openrouter/free\",\r\n    \"messages\": messages,  # Includes preserved reasoning_details\r\n    \"reasoning\": {\"enabled\": True}\r\n  })\r\n)\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-21T21:29:43+03:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":230,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T18:29:43Z","thinking":"**Assessing User's Frustration**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the core of the user's issue. Their script yielded \"0 match,\" a stark contrast to ChatGPT's earlier success. I must determine why the script underperformed. Is it a data discrepancy, a coding flaw, or a misunderstanding of the matching criteria? Digging deeper into the user's specific context is next.\n\n\n**Investigating Request Failures**\n\nI'm now checking the OpenRouter requests. The user suspects an API issue, and I'm comparing the old code and results. The `openrouter/free` model might be the problem. I'm focusing on the JSON formatting and prompt interpretation, specifically the potential for errors with the compressed `{\"s\": \"m\"}` instruction, which some open-source models may not handle well.\n\n\n**Refining Open Source Compatibility**\n\nI'm now prioritizing the compatibility issue with generic Open Source models on OpenRouter. I suspect our compressed JSON keys are the culprit. Open Source models need much clearer and explicit JSON schemas. My strategy is to revert to a human-readable format.\n```json\n{\"results\": [ {\"case_id\": \"Q123\", \"matched\": true, \"details\": \"explanation\"}, ... ]}\n```\nThis should prevent misinterpretation and empty returns.\n\n\n**Analyzing Token Limits**\n\nI've realized that the small open-source models available on `openrouter/free` struggle with handling large inputs. Even if the output token limit isn't an issue, their attention mechanisms are limited. My revised strategy is to reduce the `batch_size` back to 50 for more manageable prompts, ensuring each request stays within the model's capacity. Clear, human-readable JSON formatting with `case_id`, `status`, and `item_ids` is still crucial. I've also removed `response_format` since many free models on OpenRouter don't support it well. I'm focused on robust prompting instead.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nMain Coordinator - Matches shortages against all warehouses.\\nUses three phases: Exact Text -> Fuzzy -> LLM (OpenRouter)\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nimport time\\nimport getpass\\nimport os\\nimport re\\nimport requests as http_requests\\n\\nfrom ..config import Config\\nfrom .text_match import normalize_text, find_candidates\\n\\n\\nSYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a pharmaceutical matching assistant.\\nCompare requested pharmaceutical product descriptions with a supplied catalog.\\n\\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object matching this exact schema:\\n{\\n  \\\"results\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"case_id\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"match or no_match or review\\\",\\n      \\\"item_ids\\\": [\\\"string\\\"]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\nRules:\\n1. \\\"match\\\" means the exact same product, strength, dosage form, and pack size. Return the ID in \\\"item_ids\\\".\\n2. \\\"no_match\\\" means no exact or highly plausible match exists. \\\"item_ids\\\" must be empty [].\\n3. \\\"review\\\" means there is a plausible candidate but details are ambiguous or slightly mismatched.\\n4. DO NOT return markdown blocks. Return ONLY the raw JSON starting with { and ending with }.\\n5. ONLY return results for cases you are provided.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass Coordinator:\\n    def __init__(self, config: Config):\\n        self.config = config\\n        self.openrouter_api_key = getattr(config, 'openrouter_api_key', None)\\n\\n    def process(\\n        self,\\n        shortage_items: list[dict],\\n        warehouse_data: dict[str, list[dict]],\\n    ) -> dict:\\n        \\n        unique_shortages = {}\\n        for item in shortage_items:\\n            name = item.get(\\\"item_name_raw\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n            if name and name not in unique_shortages:\\n                unique_shortages[name] = item\\n                \\n        deduped_shortages = list(unique_shortages.value